"Dependencies) : il trouve une construction quels que soient la forme des "
"mots, leur ordre et les mots insérés. Une case vide * montre les lemmes qui "
"la remplissent. L’analyse syntaxique est automatique : elle manque des "
"occurrences et en trouve de fausses."
msgstr ""
"A schema links lemmas by syntactic relations (Universal Dependencies): it "
"finds a construction whatever the form of the words, their order and the "
"words inserted. An open slot * shows the lemmas that fill it. The syntactic "
"analysis is automatic: it misses occurrences and finds false ones."

#: templates/phraseology/schema_search.html:26
msgid ""
"Relations les plus utiles : obj (objet), nsubj (sujet), nsubj:pass (sujet "
"d’un passif), obl (complément du verbe), amod (adjectif épithète), advmod "
"(adverbe), nmod (complément du nom), case (préposition), xcomp (infinitif "
"complément)."
msgstr ""
"Most useful relations: obj (object), nsubj (subject), nsubj:pass (subject of "
"a passive), obl (adverbial), amod (attributive adjective), advmod (adverb), "
"nmod (noun modifier), case (preposition), xcomp (infinitive complement)."

